## Why This Question Is Asked
Evaluates the ability to design real-world, latency-constrained explainability systems that balance privacy and governance requirements in high-stakes ML environments.

## Key Concepts
- Per-instance explanations under strict latency constraints
- Privacy-preserving attribution without raw feature exposure
- Caching, bucketing, and surrogate models for performance optimization
- Drift monitoring and governance compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
function attribution(event) {
  const bucket = features.map(f => bucketize(f.value, f.schema));
  const fingerprint = hash(bucket);
  const cached = cache.get(fingerprint);
  if (cached) return cached;
  const attribution = surrogate.predict(bucket);
  cache.set(fingerprint, attribution);
  return attribution;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests building a scalable, privacy-preserving, multi-tenant ML platform with end-to-end governance, not just a single model. It emphasizes per-tenant isolation, drift monitoring, fairness constraints, and safe rollout strategies in production.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation and data governance
- Privacy-preserving techniques (DP/FL)
- Drift detection and alerting
- Fairness and per-tenant constraints
- Offline/online evaluation and canary rollouts
- Observability and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
function driftScore(distA, distB) {
  // simplistic KL-divergence proxy
  let s = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < distA.length; i++) {
    const a = distA[i] + 1e-9, b = distB[i] + 1e-9;
    s += a * Math.log(a / b);
  }
  return s;
}
```

